        "body": "Fathom is a San Francisco-based, for-profit public company (ticker: FTHM) founded in 2020 that operates an AI-powered meeting notetaker available at fathom.video. The company describes its core product as a tool that captures, transcribes, and summarizes calls on Zoom, Google Meet, and Microsoft Teams, with a free tier for individuals and paid features aimed at teams.\n\nThe Fathom product includes automatic action items, AI-generated summaries that can be tailored to a team's workflow, and CRM synchronization that pushes call data to connected business tools without manual input. The site also highlights an \"Ask Fathom\" search interface for querying meeting content, and AI Scorecards intended to give managers coaching metrics and performance insights from call recordings.\n\nThe held facts add that Fathom publishes an MCP server, listed as ai.fathom.api/mcp, described as giving AI assistants real meeting context so that outputs are grounded in a user's actual work. No litigation is recorded against the company in the held data.",
